        "original_id": "1f05862e-bfcc-52c9-84ee-e75a6daf4bfc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Juniper, Indigofera\n- Taxonomy: Juniperus, Cupressaceae, Fabaceae\n- Places: James Wild Horse Trap\n- Structures: corral, fences\n\nFacts:\n- Junipers are coniferous plants in the genus Juniperus of the cypress family Cupressaceae.\n- Indigofera is a large genus of more than 750 species of flowering plants in the family Fabaceae.\n- James Wild Horse Trap was the location of a corral and fences used to capture wild horses, and those structures were built from dead juniper trees.",
